OK, I just wanted to make sure. You definitely have a "NoName" board.
Quoting from the (SGML source) docs:

 <para>NoNames can either have SRM <emphasis>or</emphasis> ARC console
      firmware in their Flash ROM.  The Flash ROM is not big enough to
      hold both ARC and SRM at the same time and allow software
      selection of alternate console code. But you only need SRM
      anyway.</para>
            
In short: you need to flash the console code to SRM, ARC & SRM
won't fit together. After you did that you can install FreeBSD.

This info & more is on the FreeBSD Alpha CD, I think it is in 
the rootdir of the CD (*.TXT ??)


